{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083747-advice-needed-updating-tomb-of-dreams-for-experienced-solars","id":1083747,"title":"[Advice needed] - Updating Tomb of Dreams for experienced Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T16:34:52-07:00","id":1083747,"title":"[Advice needed] - Updating Tomb of Dreams for experienced Solars","content":"Quick background: I just started a new Exalted campaign. My players asked to start as experienced Solars, so I let them. This is our third campaign in the new edition, so I expected some understanding of the core system.<br /> <br /> In our second session, I needed a quick 'dungeon crawl' scenario, so I thought I would pull out the Tomb of Dreams. <br /> <br /> The first encounter, against the Wolf Emanation, did not go as planned. The least combat capable person, the Craft supernal Twilight, managed to fight the wolf solo. He is a grappler in combat, and crashed the wolf in approximately 2 rounds using a basic withering throw then following up with a withering Crashing Wave Throw. He blew a bunch of essence to do so, but ended up with over 30 initiative, so would likely have one shot the wolf in the subsequent round.<br /> <br /> This bodes poorly that the subsequent encounters will prove challenging for my players, especially any of the more experienced ones.<br /> <br /> Has anyone experimented yet with upping the power level of the quick start? What suggestions do you have to increase the difficulty? <br /> <br /> I've thought about adding in some battle groups with the emanations and maybe upping their stats some. However, I want challenging, not 'meatgrinder', but I'm still having trouble managing the balance of encounters in the new system. Any suggestions would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> This one is for all my Exigents...","edited":{"userid":102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","user":"LordWyrmsBane","date":".  Spelling error 04-25-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","name":"LordWyrmsBane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:09:47-07:00","id":1084000,"title":"","content":"First, rename it to Tomb of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> Second, match that new motif.<br /> <br /> First thing that jumped into my mind for Final Form, would be that any tentacles slain instantly spawn two more. Once players have accidentally multiplied the opposing force some, they'll realize they should attempt to subdue via custom gambits rather than pummel.<br /> <br /> A demon of nightmares has been forced into its own dream for millennia, and has been growing from the feedback.<br /> <br /> Freddy Kruger this shit.<br /> <br /> On that level, have the River Goddess story progress a little. While she once thought herself the Warden, as the demon has grown in strength, she is now a tormented prisoner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}